layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "For Publishers — Grosby Group"
seo_title: "For Publishers — Grosby Group | Editorial Images for Latin America"
seo_description: "Access millions of editorial images — celebrity, sports, fashion, breaking news — cleared and licensed for Latin American and US Hispanic publishers. Open an account today."
permalink: /publishers/
lang: en
faq:
  - question: "How do I get access to Grosby Group's image library?"
    answer: "Open a licensed account by clicking Get Access. Our team will review your request and set you up with credentials to browse and license content. Most accounts are activated within one business day."
  - question: "What content categories are available?"
    answer: "Celebrity, entertainment, sports, fashion and street style, travel, food and recipes, editorial news, and exclusive archival content. We represent more than 21 of the world's leading photo agencies, giving you access to tens of millions of images across every editorial category."
  - question: "How are images licensed?"
    answer: "All images are licensed for editorial use in print and digital publications. Licenses are issued on a per-use basis. Our team can also arrange exclusive territory licenses for high-demand content — contact us to discuss your needs."
  - question: "Can I get content for the US Hispanic market as well as Latin America?"
    answer: "Yes. Grosby Group covers both Latin America and the US Hispanic market. Our licensing agreements are structured to include both territories, so you don't need to negotiate separately for each."
  - question: "How quickly can I get images for a breaking story?"
    answer: "Our team monitors breaking news around the clock. For urgent editorial needs, contact us directly and we will prioritize your request. Established account holders can download images immediately from the archive platform."
  - question: "What file formats and resolutions are available?"
    answer: "Images are delivered as high-resolution JPEG files, suitable for both print and digital use. Most images are available at publication quality (300 dpi or greater). Contact your account manager if you have specific technical requirements."
